        {
          "ruleId": "api-audit/CWE-307/src/routes/users.js/login-signup-rate-limit",
          "ruleIndex": 1,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Needs validation: No rate limiting or lockout on POST /api/users/login and /signup (online password guessing; synchronous scrypt blocks the event loop). Blockers: Whether anything in front of the deployment (reverse proxy, WAF, API gateway, platform firewall) rate-limits POST /api/users/login and POST /api/users/signup before traffic reaches Node, and whether that limit is per IP or per account. Validation plan: Against staging (or production with written authorization), using a test account you own: (1) Check edge config (nginx limit_req, Cloudflare/AWS WAF rate rules, gateway throttling) for rules on the two paths. (2) From one IP send 200 POST /api/users/login with the test email and wrong passwords over ~60 s. All 401 with no 429/block/slowdown -> confirmed; 429s or blocks after N requests -> mitigated at the edge (record as rejected, ruled out by that rule). (3) Repeat from a second IP after the first is blocked: if it succeeds, the limit is per IP only and distributed guessing remains (stays confirmed at reduced likelihood). (4) While sending ~50 concurrent signups with random emails, poll GET /healthz from another client: latency well above baseline that recovers when load stops confirms the event-loop exhaustion path."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/routes/users.js",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
